{"skill": "Tenses", "difficulty": "Hard", "question": "A student analyzing the psychological torment of Roderick Usher in The Fall of the House of Usher wrote the following:

"Roderick suffered from overwhelming anxiety, and he believes the crumbling mansion amplifies his dread by echoing every whisper of his trembling voice."

Which choice best maintains a consistent verb tense in this sentence?", "choices": ["A) Roderick suffers from overwhelming anxiety, and he believed the crumbling mansion amplified his dread by echoing every whisper of his trembling voice.", "B) Roderick suffered from overwhelming anxiety, and he believed the crumbling mansion will amplify his dread by echoing every whisper of his trembling voice.", "C) Roderick suffers from overwhelming anxiety, and he believes the crumbling mansion amplifies his dread by echoing every whisper of his trembling voice.", "D) Roderick had suffered from overwhelming anxiety, and he believes the crumbling mansion amplified his dread by echoing every whisper of his trembling voice."], "answer": "C", "explanation": "To maintain consistency, both parts of the sentence should use the present tense because the description is framed as a current, ongoing situation. Choice C keeps the verbs suffers, believes, and amplifies in the same tense. In contrast, the incorrect choices switch between past, present, and future tenses in a way that disrupts the logical sequence of events.", "topic": "The psychological torment of Roderick Usher in The Fall of the House of Usher"}

P2-Revised JSON:
{"skill": "Tenses", "difficulty": "Hard", "question": "A student analyzing the psychological torment of Roderick Usher in The Fall of the House of Usher wrote the following:

"Roderick suffers from overwhelming anxiety, and the crumbling mansion, along with its eerie echoes, ______ his dread by echoing every whisper of his trembling voice."

Which choice best maintains a consistent verb tense and correct subject–verb agreement in this sentence?", "choices": ["A) amplifies", "B) amplify", "C) amplified", "D) amplifying"], "answer": "A", "explanation": "To maintain consistent verb tense, the verb must agree with the subject "the crumbling mansion" and align with the present tense 'suffers'. The subject 'the crumbling mansion' is singular, so the verb must be 'amplifies' (singular form in present tense). Choices B and D are incorrect because they use the plural verb form 'amplify', and choice C mistakenly shifts to past tense.", "topic": "The psychological torment of Roderick Usher in The Fall of the House of Usher"}

